+/-! ### LEMMA patch 0001: sound `Nat` lowering
+
+Upstream lowered `Nat` to wrapping 64-bit arithmetic and truncated `Nat` literals modulo
+2^64, so compiled code could silently disagree with the Lean definitions that proofs are
+about. With this patch, every `Nat` value held in a register is the exact mathematical value
+(always `< 2^64`), or the program has aborted:
+
+* literals `≥ 2^64` are a compile-time error,
+* `Nat.add` / `Nat.mul` abort (Solana `abort` syscall) on overflow,
+* `Nat.sub` saturates at 0, `Nat.div x 0 = 0`, `Nat.mod x 0 = x` (exactly Lean's semantics),
+* `UIntN.ofNatTruncate` clamps instead of masking.
+
+The `abort` syscall terminates the whole instruction even from inside an outlined helper,
+unlike `exit`. See `patches/0001-sound-nat-lowering.md` and
+`Lemma/Compiler/NatLowering.lean` for the kernel-checked correctness argument. -/
+
+/-- Materialize an exact `Nat` literal, refusing to truncate values that do not fit in 64 bits. -/
+private def natLitToReg (n : Nat) : LowerM VReg := do
+  if n ≥ 2 ^ 64 then
+    throw s!"Nat literal {n} does not fit in 64 bits (LEMMA patch 0001 refuses to truncate it)"
+  let r ← freshVReg
+  emit (.constImm r n.toUInt64)
+  return r
+
+/-- Create (without switching to it) a block that unconditionally aborts the program. -/
+private def newAbortBlock : LowerM BlockId := do
+  let saved := (← get).curBlock
+  let b ← newBlock
+  switchBlock b
+  emit (.syscall none "abort" #[])
+  setTerm .unreach
+  switchBlock saved
+  return b
+
